# Before: this power-law matcher required positive integer exponents.
# forall a R+, m, n N:
#     a^m * a^n = a^(m + n)
# Natural exponents include zero; the positive-base precondition is retained.
# Now: the general natural-exponent statement verifies.
# Boundary: this rule does not admit a zero base or arbitrary complex powers.
# Gate: target/release/litex -strict -f examples/proof_nodes/equal/by_builtin_rule/power_product_same_base_zero_exponent.lit

forall a R+, m, n N:
    a^m * a^n = a^(m + n)
